This app needs helper functions for users. Things that would be useful to most audio engineers. 
The scope of this change is just to add a bunch of useful constructs that users can automaticaly use with function calls
many might be pure functions, some might automatically call on members of the waviate structs. 
For example, users should have automatic access to several periodic functions. saw, square, sine, semicircle, triangle, saw tan, triangle tan, pulse, etc. between -1 and 1 with periods of 1 in the input.
there should be some cool periodic ones that are unique. saw tan is already a cool one. basically a tangent function but it wraps from -1 to 1 and vice versa. triangle tan is similar but it reflects about y = 1 and y = -1 when passing these instead of wrapping to alternate values.
Another one i'd like is a fractal square and a strong sine. the strong sine will use the 1/3 harmonic to get that kind of major third added bass that EDM artists use alot to get punchier basses. The fractal square is when x \in [0,0.5), f(x) = 1. when x \in [0.5,3/4), f(x)=-1. when x \in [3/4,7/8), f(x)=1. it alternates for each remaining half. you can use a fancy floating point trick to achieve this O(1) efficiently on a processor. 
There should also be an implementation of common coherent noises all 1d. like perlin, simplex, voronoi, turbulence, ridged multi all between 0 and 1.
Then some common audio utils people would find helpful: stuff like ADSR(a, d, s, r, t); that outputs values between 0 and 1 based on the frames for a key that's been pressed or something like that
This change isn't about implementing functions for raw values passed to the waviate structs like time since midi note was pressed or stuff like that.
It's about giving users highly expressive functions to give waviate a unique sound.